1
00:00:00,188 --> 00:00:06,376
Hello, my name is Ritesh. Aaj hum baat karenge Linear Algebra ke ek bahut interesting topic:

2
00:00:06,657 --> 00:00:11,815
Eigenvalues and Eigenvectors ke bare mein. Jab bhi koi matrix space par apply hota hai,

3
00:00:12,377 --> 00:00:16,784
toh wo sab kuch rotate aur stretch kar deta hai. Saare vectors apni direction kho dete hain.

4
00:00:16,878 --> 00:00:22,785
Lekin beech mein kuch special axes hote hain jo bilkul nahi ghumte; direction same rehti hai.

5
00:00:23,160 --> 00:00:28,411
Inhi invariant directions ko Eigenvectors kehte hain, aur scaling factor ko Eigenvalue.

6
00:00:29,068 --> 00:00:34,319
Bridges ko resonance se bachana ho, Google PageRank ho, ya data compression —

7
00:00:34,412 --> 00:00:38,819
har jagah Eigenvectors aur Eigenvalues ka concept apply hota hai.

8
00:00:39,282 --> 00:00:43,582
Ab hum log iski exact definition ko dekhte hain.

9
00:00:43,682 --> 00:00:50,582
Normally ek n x n matrix A kisi vector x se multiply hota hai, toh naya vector Ax banta hai.

10
00:00:51,282 --> 00:00:55,582
Uske angle aur length dono change ho jaate hain, jaisa left box mein dikh raha hai.

11
00:00:55,682 --> 00:01:02,582
Lekin agar koi non-zero vector v golden equation Av = lambda v satisfy kare, toh magic hota hai:

12
00:01:02,682 --> 00:01:07,682
Matrix multiplication simplify ho kar ek simple scalar scaling ban jaati hai.

13
00:01:08,082 --> 00:01:13,082
Yahan non-zero vector v hamara Eigenvector hai, aur number lambda ek Eigenvalue.

14
00:01:13,582 --> 00:01:20,582
Matlab is special line par matrix sirf ek multiplier ki tarah kaam karta hai.

15
00:01:21,082 --> 00:01:28,182
Lambda > 1 ho toh stretch, 0 aur 1 ke beech shrink, aur negative ho toh direction reverse!

16
00:01:28,823 --> 00:01:32,453
Ab iski geometry aur animation ke through samajhte hain.

17
00:01:32,645 --> 00:01:39,332
Maan lete hain hamare paas 2 x 2 matrix A hai: first row [2, 1] aur second row [1, 2].

18
00:01:39,619 --> 00:01:43,918
Pehle left graph mein red vector u = [1, 0] ko dekhte hain.

19
00:01:44,109 --> 00:01:52,325
Matrix apply hote hi ye [2, 1] par aa jaata hai (~26 degrees tilt). Matlab ye eigenvector nahi hai.

20
00:01:52,707 --> 00:01:56,624
Ab dhyan se dekho jaise unit circle stretch ho kar ek ellipse ban raha hai!

21
00:01:56,911 --> 00:02:02,548
Ab diagonal line y = x par agar hum vector v1 = [1, 1] lete hain,

22
00:02:02,834 --> 00:02:13,725
toh ye bina rotate hue bilkul isi line ke along 3 times stretch ho kar [3, 3] par pahunch jaata hai.

23
00:02:14,967 --> 00:02:22,992
Ye ellipse ki major axis hai, aur pehli eigenvalue lambda1 = 3.

24
00:02:23,852 --> 00:02:31,018
Ab yellow colour ki perpendicular line y = -x par vector v2 = [-1, 1] bilkul change nahi hua.

25
00:02:31,400 --> 00:02:40,380
Na length badli na angle (1x minor axis), toh doosri eigenvalue lambda2 = 1 hai.

26
00:02:40,953 --> 00:02:48,405
Notice karo ye dono eigenvectors 90 degrees par hain, aur yahi space ka natural skeleton banate hain.

27
00:02:48,900 --> 00:02:56,379
Par exam ya coding mein bina graph banaye math se values kaise nikalenge? Step-by-step dekhte hain.

28
00:02:56,947 --> 00:03:02,438
First step: Av = lambda v se start karenge. Rearrange karne par (A - lambda I)v = 0 milta hai.

29
00:03:03,196 --> 00:03:13,799
Kyunki v zero nahi ho sakta, determinant det(A - lambda I) = 0 hona chahiye (Characteristic Equation).

30
00:03:14,556 --> 00:03:21,846
Ab determinant solve karke characteristic equation se lambda ki values nikalte hain.

31
00:03:22,224 --> 00:03:30,366
Jaisa aap dekh sakte ho, expand karne par (2 - lambda)^2 - 1 = 0 milta hai,

32
00:03:30,934 --> 00:03:39,265
jo quadratic equation lambda^2 - 4*lambda + 3 = 0 ban jaati hai.

33
00:03:39,644 --> 00:03:48,921
Iske factors (lambda - 3)(lambda - 1) = 0 se lambda1 = 3 aur lambda2 = 1 milta hai.

34
00:03:49,773 --> 00:03:59,809
Ab eigenvectors ke liye in values ko wapas (A - lambda I)v = 0 equation mein fill karte hain,

35
00:04:00,471 --> 00:04:02,933
aur hume dono orthogonal eigenvectors v1 = [1, 1] aur v2 = [-1, 1] mil jaate hain.

36
00:04:03,315 --> 00:04:07,572
Ab aate hain last mein Diagonalization: A = P D P^-1 par.

37
00:04:07,959 --> 00:04:13,376
Normal x, y axes mein matrix A variables ko aapas mein mix kar deta hai, jisse calculation mushkil hoti hai.

38
00:04:13,859 --> 00:04:22,856
Lekin coordinate system v1, v2 par shift karne se A ek simple diagonal matrix D = diag(3, 1) ban jaata hai.

39
00:04:23,436 --> 00:04:33,013
Practical use: Maan lo kisi bridge vibration ya Markov chain ke liye A^100 nikalna hai.

40
00:04:33,496 --> 00:04:46,652
Left box dekho: normal tarike se A ko 100 baar multiply karne mein bahut time, memory aur rounding errors aate hain.

41
00:04:47,039 --> 00:04:54,778
Lekin right box: eigenbasis mein A^100 nikalna sirf 1 second ka kaam hai!

42
00:04:55,648 --> 00:05:05,322
Bas 3^100 along v1 aur 1^100 along v2 — complex problem bilkul simple scalar calculation ban jaati hai!

43
00:05:05,770 --> 00:05:15,663
End mein bas 3 points yaad rakhna: Pehla, Eigenvectors jo transformation ke baad rotate nahi hote, sirf scale hote hain.

44
00:05:16,223 --> 00:05:20,983
Doosra, Eigenvalues jo hum det(A - lambda I) = 0 solve karke nikalte hain.

45
00:05:21,263 --> 00:05:26,209
Teesra, Diagonalization jo complex matrix systems ko bilkul aasaan bana deta hai.

46
00:05:26,676 --> 00:05:33,582
Thank you so much! Ye animation video aur poora Python code maine (Ritesh Kumar) banaya.

